{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1097422-rule-question-please-help","id":1097422,"title":"Rule question, please help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-26T22:15:08-07:00","id":1097422,"title":"Rule question, please help","content":"Hey all,<br /> <br /> I'm in Alaska at a fish camp and the other people want to get a game of W:TA started. I'll ST, but I neglected to bring any of the books with me. Can someone tell me the rule about using gnosis/rage/willpower/etc in a single turn? I explained to one of the players (who, based on what I've heard him say, seems to want to stack several gifts and use them all in a single turn via rage) that there are rules about that sort of thing, but I can't remember the verbiage. <br /> <br /> Can someone help me out? I've asked that the books be sent up to me, but this will get me started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12334-chemscout","name":"Chemscout","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T23:49:47-07:00","id":1097440,"title":"","content":"You can use Willpower along with any of the other powers. But Gnosis and Rage cannot be spent on the same turn, the exception being a level 5 Glasswalker Gift Chaos Mechanics which specifically allow them to use them both together, indicating how difficult it is to do if a Gift needs to be level five and in ones tribal Wheelhouse to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T06:34:34-07:00","id":1097500,"title":"","content":"Perfect! Thank you so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12334-chemscout","name":"Chemscout","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T23:46:28-07:00","id":1097702,"title":"","content":"There are certain Gifts that require Rage and Gnosis to be spent in the same turn, and that is the other exception to the rule that they can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T07:50:13-07:00","id":1098429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1097422-rule-question-please-help?p=1097702#post1097702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are certain Gifts that require Rage and Gnosis to be spent in the same turn, and that is the other exception to the rule that they can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I like to call &quot;The Exceptional Rule of Exceptions: All rules have exceptions and thus one need not enumerate them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}